What I believe Pat is suggesting is that you score the last _started_
game to ascend; thus, if I started a game on Nov 3 and won two minutes
before Dec 1, I would lose to someone who started a game four hours
before Dec 1 and ascended five minutes before Dec 1. I think that is
more skillful in certain ways, but...

In defense of the First Ascension trophy, I find it a great way to
generate interest in the tournament on day 1, at least when it's
possible to watch; both the NAO NetHack tournaments and the August
CAO Crawl tournament had a large number of watchers waiting to see who
would finish first. I would probably follow the devnull first ascension
race by watching games even if I weren't playing, and I don't think I'm
the only one. The last ascension race would have a similar effect, but
anyone who got excited about it wouldn't then be able to say "Oh yes,
I will join in the tournament! This is too fun to miss!"

The main problems I see with the First Ascension trophy are these:

 * It penalizes people by time zone (also true of last ascension, though)
 * It can be problematic if there are bugs with the new challenge code
   (the teleporting caused by undead on Nov 1 last year was entertaining, 
   but not exactly an ideal condition :) --- this would be fixed by having
   the race at the end
 * It can do weird things to what bonesfiles show up, and starts the race
   with ~no bones in place; this is probably not a big problem, but I wanted
   a third thing for the list

You could always do both!

I'm unlikely to play much this year (full time work and full time grad
school will do that) but I totally support the First Ascension trophy and
look forward to watching the outcome of the tournament. As always, thanks
for organizing it. :) 

